\title{killerPals: Colourblind-Friendly Colour Palettes Inspired by Queen Album Covers}
\description{
\if{html}{\figure{logo.png}{options: style='float: right' alt='logo' width='120'}}

Forty-eight colour palettes derived from the fifteen Queen studio album covers, with qualitative, sequential and diverging variants for every album. Palettes are optimised so that their worst-case pairwise CIEDE2000 separation stays high under simulated deuteranopic, protanopic and tritanopic vision, and so that every colour clears a minimum contrast ratio against light and dark backgrounds. Sequential and diverging palettes are strictly monotone in lightness, so they survive greyscale printing. Includes 'ggplot2' scales for discrete, continuous and binned aesthetics, plus tools to simulate colour vision deficiency and audit any palette's accessibility.
}
